<title>RUSSIA: Russia 1,067-day bond tranche priced 100.90 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 1,067-day bond tranche priced 100.90 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of an additional tranche of a Russian 1,067-day OFZ interest-bearing bond with a fixed coupon was 100.90 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The original issue on Tuesday closed at 100.89 percent to yield 19.51 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		   25016</p>
<p>(additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    2.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		  1.74 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		     1.76 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold				620.08 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  635.51 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		   100.90 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	 100.90 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		    19.51 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	 19.51 pct</p>
<p>    Original issue date	   July 10, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	     1,067 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   June 10, 2000</p>
<p>    Coupon rate		     20 pct</p>
<p>    First coupon date	     June 10, 1998</p>
<p>    Accruals			  15,890.41 rbls</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry on Wednesday will offer four trillion roubles in an additional tranche of 686-day bond (series 24013).</p>
<p>It will also repay 4.59 trillion roubles in maturing 18-month bonds (series 24005) and 354.39 billion roubles in interest on the bond.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
